swer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71e29f52-5060-5d27-9c9d-18f7d7566204" :answer/id #uuid "71e29f52-5060-5d27-9c9d-18f7d7566204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(C)=-1\\notin C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b532e7e-fcc3-5f04-a240-fffc7b69c0f1" :answer/id #uuid "2b532e7e-fcc3-5f04-a240-fffc7b69c0f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(C)=-2\\in C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2c87cf-ca24-56a0-8947-a8ba427cb930" :answer/id #uuid "8e2c87cf-ca24-56a0-8947-a8ba427cb930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(C)=-2\\notin C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aeeaf2b-e22f-5929-a602-8a420267ddc3" :answer/id #uuid "5aeeaf2b-e22f-5929-a602-8a420267ddc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$sup(C)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f25266f1-2830-5a2e-9d12-da4f0e084a1d" :question/id #uuid "f25266f1-2830-5a2e-9d12-da4f0e084a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-253561" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=(-\\infty ,\\pi \\,].$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(B)$ and $sup(B).$\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(B)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(B)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $B.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSince $B$ is unbounded below, $B$ has no lower bounds, and $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge \\pi $ is greater than or equal to the elements of $B.$ Thus, the set $[\\pi ,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $B.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<\\pi $ is **not** an upper bound of $B.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $B$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, $[\\pi ,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $B,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(B)=min\\,[\\pi ,\\infty )=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $B$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $B,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{unbounded below},$ we have $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{bounded above},$ we have $sup(B)=\\pi .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a40b4703-dfd5-5604-aa4e-aadffb8912d4" "answer-field-0141976c-ee04-53f0-9dd6-35986d4022e3" "answer-field-98631c3a-b7b8-5e51-9528-4755eb8c1bc1" "answer-field-66105b1a-13c8-5513-a373-da34de27abfb" "answer-field-f44a72e2-fb07-5479-a992-4153e0e61bf3" "answer-field-78ca7332-89ea-5659-a5d1-daae2fcaf25a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a40b4703-dfd5-5604-aa4e-aadffb8912d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a40b4703-dfd5-5604-aa4e-aadffb8912d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-94c16107-81fc-53a0-9f76-3bb3d8bfa2e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94c16107-81fc-53a0-9f76-3bb3d8bfa2e8" "answer-201ceafe-9cde-510e-94f6-947e5d6472b9" "answer-63734a92-b3f1-59c8-9eb8-2fd264d2bb50" "answer-aa2db595-99a3-57f2-9df2-ccb0175a7e84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94c16107-81fc-53a0-9f76-3bb3d8bfa2e8" :answer/id #uuid "94c16107-81fc-53a0-9f76-3bb3d8bfa2e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201ceafe-9cde-510e-94f6-947e5d6472b9" :answer/id #uuid "201ceafe-9cde-510e-94f6-947e5d6472b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest upper 